{
  "version": 2,
  "_comment": [
    "The tile catalogue. This is the file to edit for an L2 change (build plan section 6):",
    "change a number here, run `python3 scripts/tilegen.py`, then `ttsd.py call reskin`.",
    "",
    "Cells are axial (q, r) on a pointy-top lattice, relative to the tile's pivot,",
    "which is always the cell at (0, 0). The trihex shape reproduces the geometry",
    "measured from Railways of the Lost Atlas: hexes at (0,0), (-1,1) and (0,1),",
    "which in world units is (0,0), (-sqrt(3)/2, 1.5) and (+sqrt(3)/2, 1.5).",
    "",
    "A FLAT kind draws GREYSCALE on purpose. Colour comes from ColorDiffuse at",
    "runtime, so recolouring a kind is a live tint (L1) and not a regenerate.",
    "It takes that tint from `terrains` when it shares a terrain's name.",
    "",
    "A PAINTED kind (one with a `paint` block) bakes colour in and drops to L2:",
    "terrain changes inside the tile, and one ColorDiffuse cannot express two",
    "terrains. Edit a colour in `terrains`, regenerate, `ttsd.py call reskinall`.",
    "",
    "Edges in a `paint` block are numbered 1..6 the way src/10-hex.lua numbers",
    "directions: 1=E 2=SE 3=SW 4=W 5=NW 6=NE. Only a tile's OUTER edges may be",
    "overridden; an edge facing another cell of the same tile blends to that",
    "cell's own terrain and tilegen refuses an override on it. For the trihex",
    "the outer edges are cell 1: 1,2,3,4 | cell 2: 3,4,5,6 | cell 3: 1,2,5,6.",
    "",
    "THE OWNER NUMBERS THEM THE OTHER WAY. At the table he says 1=W 2=NW 3=NE",
    "4=E 5=SE 6=SW — clockwise from west, where this file runs anticlockwise",
    "from east. To turn one of his numbers into a spec number add 3 and wrap:",
    "his 1,2,3 are spec 4,5,6 and his 4,5,6 are spec 1,2,3. His 'first topmost'",
    "cell is the second paint entry, cell (-1,1); 'the other one' is the third,",
    "cell (0,1). In his numbering the legal outer edges are cell 1: 1,4,5,6 |",
    "cell 2: 1,2,3,6 | cell 3: 2,3,4,5."
  ],

